{% extends "base.jinja" %}
{% block head %}
    <script src="/static/js/region-guess.js"></script>
    <style>
    .nt-cl h4 { margin-top: 2rem; }
    .nt-cl ol li { margin-bottom: .35rem; }
    .nt-cl .nt-url { display: flex; gap: .5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: .4rem 0 .2rem; }
    .nt-cl .nt-url code { font-size: .95rem; word-break: break-all; }
    .nt-cl .nt-note { font-size: .88rem; opacity: .75; }
    .nt-cl pre { background: rgba(127, 127, 127, .12); padding: .6rem .8rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: .82rem; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }
    </style>
{% endblock head %}
{% block body %}
<div class="container nt-cl" style="max-width: 900px">
    <h2>Use the trackers in your torrent client</h2>
    <p>More trackers means more peers and faster downloads, especially for older or less popular torrents.
       The best way is to give your client this site's list <b>as a link</b>, so it stays up to date by itself.</p>

    <p class="mb-0"><b>Your list</b> (working trackers, fast from <span id="nt-where">anywhere</span>):</p>
    <div class="nt-url"><code id="nt-list">https://newtrackon.co.nz/api/clean</code>
        <button id="nt-copy" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Copy</button></div>
    <p class="nt-note">For a different region or other options, see the <a href="/list">List</a> page.</p>

    <h4 id="qbittorrent">qBittorrent</h4>
    <ol>
        <li>Open <b>Tools &rarr; Options &rarr; BitTorrent</b> (on a Mac: <b>qBittorrent &rarr; Preferences &rarr; BitTorrent</b>).</li>
        <li>Tick <b>Automatically append trackers from URL to new downloads</b> and paste your list link into the box.</li>
        <li>Click <b>OK</b>. New torrents get the trackers from then on.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="nt-note">Older versions don't have that option: tick <b>Automatically add these trackers to new downloads</b> instead
       and paste the list itself (open the link, copy everything). That copy won't update, so redo it now and then.
       Torrents added from the command line while qBittorrent isn't running don't get the URL trackers.</p>

    <h4 id="transmission">Transmission (4.0 or later)</h4>
    <p>Transmission has a <code>default-trackers</code> setting, added to all public torrents. It's set in
       <code>settings.json</code> (the GTK app, the daemon and the command-line version; not the Mac app):</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Quit Transmission (or stop the daemon): it rewrites <code>settings.json</code> on exit.</li>
        <li>Open the list link and copy the trackers into <code>"default-trackers"</code>, separated by <code>\n\n</code>
            typed literally inside the quotes, as in the example below (real line breaks would break the file).</li>
        <li>Start Transmission again.</li>
    </ol>
    <pre>"default-trackers": "udp://tracker.example.org:1337/announce\n\nhttps://tracker.example.net:443/announce",</pre>
    <p class="nt-note">Like a pasted list, this one doesn't update by itself.</p>

    <h4 id="deluge">Deluge</h4>
    <p>Deluge can't do it on its own, but the <a href="https://github.com/stefantalpalaru/deluge-default-trackers">Default Trackers</a>
       plugin can: it adds trackers to new public torrents (never to private ones) and can reload them from a link.</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Install the plugin (<b>Preferences &rarr; Plugins &rarr; Install Plugin</b>, using the file for your Deluge's Python version)
            and enable it.</li>
        <li>In <b>Preferences &rarr; Default Trackers</b>, add your list link as the URL to load.</li>
    </ol>

    <h4 id="other">Any other client, or one download</h4>
    <p>Most clients let you add trackers to a torrent in its properties or <b>Trackers</b> tab: paste the list there.
       Or use <a href="/tools">Tools</a>: paste a magnet link or open a .torrent file, and get it back with the best trackers added.</p>

    <h4>Private trackers</h4>
    <p>Don't add public trackers to torrents from a private tracker: it's against their rules and can get your account banned.
       qBittorrent, Transmission and the Deluge plugin all leave private torrents alone, and so do the Tools here.</p>
</div>
<script>
(function () {
    var r = typeof ntGuessRegion === 'function' ? ntGuessRegion() : '';
    var url = 'https://newtrackon.co.nz/api/clean' + (r ? '?fast_from=' + r : '');
    document.getElementById('nt-list').textContent = url;
    if (r && typeof NT_REGION_NAMES !== 'undefined') { document.getElementById('nt-where').textContent = NT_REGION_NAMES[r]; }
    document.getElementById('nt-copy').addEventListener('click', function () {
        var b = this;
        (navigator.clipboard ? navigator.clipboard.writeText(url) : Promise.reject()).then(function () { b.textContent = 'Copied'; },
            function () { b.textContent = 'Select and copy it'; });
    });
})();
</script>
{% endblock %}
